.TH ZOSEZA 1 "November 2026" "zoseza 1.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zoseza \- modern eza-inspired file listing utility for IBM z/OS USS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zoseza.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
[\fIPATH\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zoseza
is a feature-rich Python implementation inspired by the
.B eza
directory listing utility and tailored specifically for IBM z/OS UNIX
System Services (USS).
.PP
It combines modern file listing capabilities with z/OS-specific features
including colorized terminal output, EBCDIC and ASCII file tag awareness
(\fBchtag\fR), extended attribute inspection (\fBextattr\fR), POSIX ACL
indicator detection (\fB+\fR), zFS dataset resolution (\fBdf\fR), and Git
repository integration.
.PP
In addition to a traditional command-line interface,
.B zoseza
provides an interactive full-screen Text User Interface (TUI) for
browsing, sorting, filtering, dynamically adding or removing display
columns, inspecting, viewing files in ASCII/EBCDIC/Hex, modifying z/OS
attributes (\fBchtag\fR, \fBextattr\fR, \fBchmod\fR), editing, and managing
files directly on the mainframe.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I paths
One or more files or directories to display (default: current directory).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-all
Show hidden files (entries starting with \fB.\fR). The parent directory
(\fB..\fR) is pinned to the top of directory listings.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-long
Display extended metadata (permissions, ACL indicator, hard links, owner,
group, size, and timestamp).
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-git
Display Git status badges for entries and show the active Git branch in
directory headers.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time
Sort entries by modification time (newest first). Combine with \fB\-u\fR
or \fB\-c\fR to sort by access or status change time.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-access
Display last access time (\fBatime\fR) in long view, and sort by access
time when combined with \fB\-t\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-ctime
Display status change time (\fBctime\fR) in long view, and sort by status
change time when combined with \fB\-t\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-icons
Display Nerd Font file-type icons next to filenames.
.TP
.B \-\-inode
Display the file serial number (inode).
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-octal
Display file permissions in 4-digit octal format alongside symbolic
permissions in long view.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-numeric
Display numeric user IDs (UID) and group IDs (GID) instead of resolved
names.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-blocks
Calculate and display file sizes using 512-byte block allocations
instead of exact byte counts.
.TP
.BI "\-J, \-\-json " FILE
Export the directory listing and metadata as structured JSON to \fIFILE\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-e, \-\-ext " EXT
Filter files by a comma-separated list of file extensions (for example,
\fBtxt,rex,py\fR). Directories are still shown during traversal.
.TP
.BI "\-R, \-\-regex " PATTERN
Filter files matching the specified regular expression \fIPATTERN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-tags
Display z/OS USS file tag state (\fBt\fR, \fBb\fR, \fBm\fR, \fB\-\fR)
and character codeset (such as \fBIBM-1047\fR or \fBISO8859-1\fR).
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-extattr
Display z/OS extended attributes in \fB[apsl]\fR badge format (APF
authorized, program controlled, shared address space, shared library).
.TP
.B \-\-tree
Display directories and their contents in a recursive tree hierarchy.
.TP
.BI "\-L, \-\-level " DEPTH
Limit the recursion depth when displaying a directory tree with \fB\-\-tree\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-group\-directories\-first
List directories before regular files across any active sort order.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-directory
List directories themselves rather than their contents.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sort\-size
Sort entries by file size (largest first).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reverse
Reverse the active sort order.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-oneline
Display one entry per line.
.TP
.BR \-D ", " \-\-dsn
Show underlying zFS dataset names in brackets. To reduce visual clutter,
the dataset name is displayed on the first entry and whenever an entry
resides on a different zFS dataset than the preceding line.
.TP
.BI "\-\-color " WHEN
Specify when to use terminal colors: \fBauto\fR (default; colors enabled
only on TTY output), \fBalways\fR, or \fBnever\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable all terminal colors (alias for \fB\-\-color=never\fR).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display program version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Launch the interactive full-screen curses Text User Interface.
.SH TUI HOTKEYS
When running with \fB\-\-tui\fR, each hotkey is listed below in a
single-column reference:
.TP
.B UP / DOWN
Move the selection cursor up or down line by line.
.TP
.B PgUp / PgDn
Scroll the directory listing or built-in file viewer by a full page.
.TP
.B Home / End
Jump immediately to the first or last entry in the directory or file viewer.
.TP
.B ENTER
Enter the selected directory or open the selected file in the built-in
viewer (which supports live ASCII, EBCDIC \fBIBM-1047\fR, and Hex dump
toggles).
.TP
.B ESC
Navigate up to the parent directory, or close active sub-views and dialogs
(configured with a fast 25ms escape delay).
.TP
.B .
Toggle display of hidden dotfiles (\fB\-a\fR).
.TP
.B d
Toggle grouping directories before regular files (\fB[Dirs1st]\fR).
.TP
.B i
Open the full-screen File Info inspector showing complete POSIX metadata,
z/OS file tags, extended attributes, ACL entries, zFS dataset, mount
point, timestamps, and Git status.
.TP
.B e
Edit the selected file using the configured editor (\fB$EDITOR\fR or
\fBvi\fR).
.TP
.B m
Create a new directory (\fBmkdir\fR) via a centered popup input dialog.
.TP
.B A
Create a new empty file via a centered popup input dialog.
.TP
.B p
Change file permissions (\fBchmod\fR) using a centered popup dialog
pre-filled with the file's current 4-digit octal mode.
.TP
.B u
Change the z/OS USS file tag (\fBchtag\fR) using a centered popup menu
supporting \fBISO8859-1\fR, \fBIBM-1047\fR, \fBUTF-8\fR, custom codesets,
binary (\fB\-b\fR), mixed (\fB\-m\fR), or tag removal (\fB\-r\fR).
.TP
.B x
Modify z/OS extended attributes (\fBextattr\fR) using an interactive
checklist modal for \fB+a\fR/\fB\-a\fR, \fB+p\fR/\fB\-p\fR,
\fB+s\fR/\fB\-s\fR, and \fB+l\fR/\fB\-l\fR.
.TP
.B C
Copy the selected file or directory using a centered, bordered popup
dialog box pre-filled with the current name.
.TP
.B R
Rename the selected file or directory using a centered, bordered popup
dialog box pre-filled with the current name.
.TP
.B D
Delete the selected file or directory after confirming in a centered
popup dialog box.
.TP
.B s
Sort entries by file size (largest first).
.TP
.B t
Sort entries by modification time (\fBmtime\fR).
.TP
.B a
Sort entries by last access time (\fBatime\fR).
.TP
.B z
Sort entries by status change time (\fBctime\fR).
.TP
.B n
Sort entries alphabetically by filename.
.TP
.B r
Reverse the current sort order.
.TP
.B f \fRor\fB /
Filter the current directory listing by substring.
.TP
.B c
Clear the active substring filter in the directory browser, or cycle file
decoding (\fBAUTO\fR, \fBISO8859-1\fR, \fBIBM-1047\fR, \fBHEX\fR) inside
the built-in File Viewer.
.TP
.B h
Toggle the side-by-side Hex / ASCII / EBCDIC (\fBIBM-1047\fR) dump view
inside the built-in File Viewer.
.TP
.B v
Open the interactive TUI Columns Menu modal to dynamically add or remove
any column (Inode, Octal, Permissions, Links, Owner, Group, Numeric IDs,
Size, 512B Blocks, Timestamp, Git Status, z/OS File Tags, ExtAttr, Icons,
and zFS Dataset). If \fBSave Columns\fR is enabled in the \fBo\fR Settings
menu, pressing \fBs\fR inside the Columns Menu saves the active column
layout to \fI~/.pyeza.json\fR.
.TP
.B I
Toggle display of Inode numbers.
.TP
.B O
Toggle display of Octal permissions.
.TP
.B N
Toggle display of Numeric UIDs and GIDs.
.TP
.B G
Toggle display of Git status badges.
.TP
.B T
Toggle display of z/OS File Tags (\fBchtag\fR).
.TP
.B X
Toggle display of z/OS Extended Attributes (\fB[apsl]\fR).
.TP
.B M
Toggle display of underlying zFS Dataset names.
.TP
.B B
Toggle display of 512-byte Block sizes.
.TP
.B W
Toggle display of Nerd Font Icons.
.TP
.B o
Open the colorized interactive Settings menu with live color previews,
popup editor configuration, the \fBSave Columns\fR toggle (default: OFF),
and save confirmation dialog.
.TP
.B F1
Display the colorized built-in TUI help screen.
.TP
.B q
Quit the current view or exit the TUI.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set (to any value), disables all ANSI and curses color output unless
overridden.
.TP
.B LS_COLORS
Colon-separated list of ANSI color mappings (\fBdi\fR, \fBex\fR, \fBln\fR,
\fBfi\fR) used to customize CLI colors.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Default text editor command used by the TUI \fBe\fR hotkey if not
overridden in \fI~/.pyeza.json\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pyeza.json
User preferences and TUI configuration file storing custom color pairs,
default editor command, and optional saved column preferences (when
\fBsave_columns\fR is enabled).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.
.TP
.B 1
Command-line argument or regular expression compilation error.
.TP
.B 130
Execution interrupted by the user (\fBCtrl+C\fR / \fBSIGINT\fR).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B zoseza.py
List files in the current directory in a multi-column grid.
.TP
.B zoseza.py \-laTgD \-\-group\-directories\-first
Show all files in long format with directories grouped first, Git status,
z/OS file tags, and underlying zFS dataset names (shown when the dataset
changes).
.TP
.B zoseza.py \-tx \-e rex,py
List REXX and Python files sorted by newest modification time alongside
z/OS extended attributes.
.TP
.B zoseza.py \-\-tree \-L 2
Display a recursive directory tree limited to 2 levels deep.
.TP
.B zoseza.py \-\-tui
Launch the interactive full-screen Text User Interface.
.SH SEE ALSO
